===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|ru|агитпро́п}}, short for {{m|ru|[[отде́л]] [[агитация|агитации]] [[и]] [[пропаганда|пропаганды]]||Department for Agitation and Propaganda}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/ˈædʒ.ɪtˌpɹɒp/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-I learned some phrases-agitprop.wav|Audio (UK)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|uncountable}} Political [[propaganda]] [[disseminate]]d through [[art]], [[literature]], [[drama]], etc., especially [[communist]] propaganda.
#* {{quote-book|en|date=June 23, 2020|author={{w|John Bolton}}|title={{w|The Room Where It Happened}}|isbn=978-1-9821-4803-4|page=96|passage=The letter was pure puffery, probably written by some clerk in North Korea's '''agitprop''' bureau, but Trump loved it.}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} An organization or person engaged in disseminating such propaganda.

